+
+# Bulk import helper importTasks
+
+## Request
+
+Teams are moving to Tidy Tasks from their spreadsheets. Add a public helper for bulk import,
+`importTasks(list, text)`, exported from `src/index.ts`.
+
+The text holds one task per line, as `title;priority;tags`:
+
+- the priority may be left empty for a normal one;
+- the tags are separated by spaces, e.g. `Renew the insurance;high;admin money`;
+- blank lines are skipped.
+
+It adds every valid line to the list and returns `{ imported, rejected }`:
+
+- `imported` is how many tasks were added;
+- `rejected` lists every line that could not be added, as `{ line, reason }`, with `line` counting
+  from 1.
+
+## Traceability
+
+- Feature: task list for the Tidy Tasks app (`README.md`), used by the teams moving from spreadsheets.
+- Requirement: a bulk import adds each valid line and reports each rejected line with its line number
+  and the reason.
+- Builds on: task-003 (validation of title, priority and tags), which `importTasks` relies on through
+  `list.add`, so a line is checked by the same rules as a single add.
+- Acceptance: covered by tests in `test/import.test.ts`.
+
+## Design
+
+- The helper lives in `src/domain/import.ts` and takes the `TaskList` to add to. It reads no clock; the
+  list stamps the tasks as usual (R3).
+- Parsing: the text is split on `\n`, and a trailing `\r` is removed. A line whose trimmed content is
+  empty is skipped, but still counts in the line numbers.
+- Each other line must have exactly three fields separated by `;`. Any other count is rejected with a
+  reason that shows the expected form. This also means a title cannot contain `;`.
+- Title: passed to `list.add` as it is; the list trims it and applies the empty, length and duplicate
+  checks. A duplicate, including one repeated from an earlier line of the same text, is rejected.
+- Priority: trimmed. Empty means `normal`. Otherwise it is passed on, so the list's priority check
+  applies and rejects anything other than `low`, `normal` or `high`.
+- Tags: split on runs of whitespace, empty pieces dropped, so an empty field means no tags. Each tag is
+  checked by `list.add`.
+- Each line is added on its own. Valid lines are kept even when other lines are rejected; the import is
+  not all-or-nothing, as the request asks for every valid line to be added.
+- The reason for a rejected line is the message the list returned for it.
+- Public API: `importTasks`, and the types `ImportResult` and `RejectedLine`, are exported from
+  `src/index.ts`. Adds to the public API only; nothing existing changes.
+- No new dependency (R1).
+
+## Notes
+
+- No credentials or secrets are involved.
+- Ambiguities settled here: whitespace around the priority is ignored; tags split on any whitespace;
+  an extra `;` makes the line invalid rather than being folded into the title.
